 "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/23/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date`, and `tests/test_parse.py` now passes (3 passed, including `test_dates`).\n\n**Fix** (`dates/parse.py`): I replaced `datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. The old format string had no way to match a trailing `Z`. `fromisoformat` reads `Z` and `\u00b1HH:MM` offsets on Python 3.11 and later; this machine has 3.13.5.\n\n**What's different now:**\n- **Timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset** now come back as timezone-aware datetimes (`tzinfo=UTC` for `Z`) instead of failing. If any code compares or subtracts these against naive datetimes, it will raise `TypeError`. The tests don't exercise that case.\n- **Timestamps with no zone** still come back naive, as before.\n- **`day_key`** returns the calendar date as written in the string, not converted to local time.\n- **Python version:** the repo has no project config file (no `pyproject.toml` or similar), so nothing declares a minimum Python version. On Python 3.10 or older, `fromisoformat` rejects `Z`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections"